# ── Database ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Supabase connection string. Use the SESSION pooler for migrations and the
# TRANSACTION pooler for the app.
#
# There is one database (docs/DEPLOY.md): this file, the GitHub secret and
# Vercel all point at it, so a value here is production. No `?sslmode=` —
# db/client.ts turns TLS on for any non-local host, and sslmode in the string
# overrides that and fails against the pooler (docs/NIGHTLY.md).
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres

# ── Encryption ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 32-byte key, hex-encoded. Generate once with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
#
# MUST BE IDENTICAL across local, preview and production — they share one
# database. If it differs, every encrypted setting becomes unreadable and the
# error looks like "Unsupported state". Never rotate it casually.
ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# ── Auth ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Signs the session cookie. Generate with `npx auth secret`.
#
# Unlike ENCRYPTION_KEY this one MAY differ between environments — a preview
# deployment having its own is fine and slightly safer. Changing it signs
# everyone out of that environment, which is also the only way to end a session
# early: sessions are JWTs, so there is no row to delete.
AUTH_SECRET=

# Only needed where the deployment URL cannot be inferred. `trustHost: true` is
# set in the auth config so Vercel preview URLs work without touching this.
AUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000

# There is no sign-up page. Create the first account with:
#   npm run user:create -- --email=you@example.com --role=admin

# ── S3 (raw page storage) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Same variable names as the Vault project so the ported client works unchanged.
S3_ENDPOINT=
S3_REGION=auto
S3_BUCKET=
S3_ACCESS_KEY=
S3_SECRET_KEY=

# ── Inngest ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
INNGEST_EVENT_KEY=
INNGEST_SIGNING_KEY=

# ── Crawling ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Identifies us to the portals that granted written permission. Keep it
# honest and reachable — several of them agreed on the basis of knowing who
# we are.
CRAWLER_USER_AGENT=PortalMonitoringAgent/1.0 (+https://leadestate.com; contact@leadestate.com)

# Same thing under the name the code reads first; wins over CRAWLER_USER_AGENT
# when both are set. collect.yml fills it from the CRAWLER_USER_AGENT secret.
#   COLLECTOR_USER_AGENT=

# The X-Collector header LuxuryEstate's permission is tied to, written into its
# source config by `npm run db:seed`. Unset means the user-agent above.
#   COLLECTOR_HEADER=

# Egress for portals that filter by address CLASS (Figaro, JamesEdition serve
# this code from a home connection and refuse datacentre ranges). A source
# opts in with `config.proxyEnv: "PMA_RESIDENTIAL_PROXY"`; the URL and its
# credentials live only here. Not for portals that refused our identity —
# see the note on `proxy` in src/lib/portals/runner/browser.ts.
#   PMA_RESIDENTIAL_PROXY=http://user:pass@gate.provider.example:7000

# Debugging only: set to 1 and Etreproprio's discovery prints one line per
# index page. Leave unset for a real night.
#   COLLECT_DEBUG_PAGES=1

# ── Stream.Estate ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The client's PAID V1 key (source `stream-estate-v1`, `npm run stream:history`).
# Billed per item returned, on the client's card: only ever used through the
# meter in src/lib/portals/streamV1.ts. Never paste it into a chat.
STREAM_ESTATE_API_KEY=

# The free V2 beta key (source `stream-estate`). A different key from the one above.
STREAM_ESTATE_V2_API_KEY=

# Not set here: NODE_ENV (Next and Vercel set it) and GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY
# (GitHub Actions sets it). The code reads both; neither belongs in this file.
